  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted fusion is the clear best combination (config_017: 0.725 acc, 3.60 GPU hrs), with transformer aggregation. The only untested variation within this top-performing family is the aggregation method (avgpool vs transformer). Question: Does the transformer aggregation provide meaningful benefit over simple average pooling for multiprofile aggregation, or is the cross-attention overkill? This is important because avgpool is substantially cheaper (no self-attention over profiles), so if it matches transformer within ~1%, we get a cost-efficient configuration. Why this is the best next step: It keeps all three proven-best components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) and isolates the single remaining architectural uncertainty in the top-performing family. With 5 experiments left, confirming or ruling out the transformer's contribution lets us either exploit a cheaper equivalent or confidently invest remaining budget in other dimensions (e.g., resnet50 image encoder, single-profile). Expected relative cost: ~2.5–3.0 GPU hours, roughly 20-30% cheaper than config_017's 3.60 hrs since avgpool replaces the transformer attention layer."
